Neovim Tutor: 01 BASICS

This is a local lesson pack stored in: ~/.config/nvim/tutor/
Open with: :Tutor nvchad-01-basics

Goal
  Learn how to move, exit, and get help without panic.

Rules
  - Read a section, then do it in THIS buffer.
  - Practice until it feels easy, then move on.

------------------------------------------------------------
Lesson 1: Modes
  Normal mode: for commands (default)
  Insert mode: for typing text
  Visual mode: for selecting

Try this now:
  - Press i to enter Insert mode and type a short sentence.
  - Press <Esc> to return to Normal mode.
  - Press v to enter Visual mode, move around, then press <Esc>.

------------------------------------------------------------
Lesson 2: Basic movement (home row)
  h  left    j  down    k  up    l  right

Practice:
  - Move to the start of the previous line with k.
  - Move to the end of the next line with j.

------------------------------------------------------------
Lesson 3: Fast movement
  w  next word
  b  previous word
  0  start of line
  $  end of line
  gg top of file
  G  bottom of file

Practice:
  - Jump to the top of this file with gg.
  - Jump to the bottom with G.

------------------------------------------------------------
Lesson 4: Undo / redo
  u   undo
  <C-r> redo

Practice:
  - Delete a line with dd, then undo with u.
  - Redo with <C-r>.

------------------------------------------------------------
Lesson 5: Quit safely
  :q      quit (fails if modified)
  :q!     quit without saving
  :wq     write and quit

Try:
  - Type :q and see the warning if modified.

------------------------------------------------------------
Lesson 6: Help
  :help
  :help motion
  :help :wq

Practice:
  - Run :help motion, then close help with :q.

End of lesson 01.
Next: :Tutor nvchad-02-editing
